WEBVTT

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:05.230
Is that all there is to your "true strength"?

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:11.790
A good gambler doesn't play 
his ace on the first hand.

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.730
As of now, it's my turn.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:20.060
How foolish. If you use Slow Down
on a wall of cards,

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.060
I only need to offset it with Speed Up!

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:22.660
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.220
So much power...

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.440
What's going on?

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.520
Well, my precious memories 
were on the line before,

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.520
so I never tested it.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.440
But now I know.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:56.020
This UNIQUE embedded in my chest

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.890
can activate both Speed Up 
and Slow Down simultaneously,

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.450
just like the latest Oath of Time models.

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.210
I see. So that's it.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:06.970
Exactly.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:10.330
I made a wall of Slowed Down cards,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.250
Slow Down x 1000

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.770
and hid some Sped Up cards behind them.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:19.430
Your Speed Up tore down my 
Slowed Down wall of cards,

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.720
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.990
but the cards behind them were even 
further Sped Up by your power.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.680
Speed Up x 500 x 1000

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.940
Speed Up x 500000

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:26.060
Speed Up x 500000

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:26.140
Speed Up x 500000

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.540
And the result was the blast you just saw.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.280
Your Oath of Time is an old model!

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:12.760
Sucks that you can't have Speed Up and Slow
Down active at the same time, doesn't it?!

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.140
Very nice! I love it!

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:18.500
Being a villain feels so great!

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.670
Time to finish this!

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.960
You take pleasure in hurting others.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.780
Is that why you call yourself a villain?

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.480
You really are simple-minded.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.870
Huh? Hurting others?

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.750
There's a lot more to my evil than that!

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:49.280
Okay, then. I'll tell you a little story.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:57.390
Once upon a time, in a small village,
there lived two children.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.260
Boy A was a good, kind boy

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.550
who always tried to help others.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:06.600
Think nothing of it, ma'am.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.150
I just want to help 
everyone as much as I can.

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:11.580
All the villagers liked him

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.170
and felt sure he'd have a bright future.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:18.980
Boy B, on the other hand, was mean and nasty.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:22.330
He spent every day making mischief 
and bullying weaker children.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:24.360
He was a nuisance to everyone.

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.820
Naturally, the villagers 
quickly gave up on Boy B.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:29.600
But...

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:36.110
Hey, you shouldn't do that.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.870
It seems like it's hurting 
you more than anyone else.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:47.920
The soft-hearted Boy A tried 
to straighten out Boy B.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:54.400
But B only felt disgusted by 
A's abnormally virtuous nature.

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.140
Then, one night,

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:02.230
B called A out with him and 
led him into the fields...

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.070
Then he burned down the windmill, 
right before A's eyes!

00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:34.140
Both boys were found at the scene, 
and the villagers were furious.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:37.420
Honestly, you again?

00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:39.650
There's just no helping you.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.880
But it wasn't B who took 
the brunt of their anger.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.360
How could you do something so terrible?

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.750
It all fell on A, who was innocent.

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:53.810
You pretended to be a good boy to fool us!

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:54.660
No!

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.330
He can't be trusted at all.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.830
What a wretched child!

00:05:57.830 --> 00:05:58.830
I was just...

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.500
Why?

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.360
Why won't you believe me?!

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:05.710
I Was Always a Good Boy

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.710
You are nothing but lying scum!

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:22.970
And so, A learned just 
how unfair this world is.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:28.240
A single incident staged to draw suspicion 
canceled out a lifetime of virtue.

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:32.050
In fact, everyone thought all 
his good deeds had been a lie,

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:37.330
making their disappointment 
and hatred even greater.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:40.040
From that day forth, Boy A decided

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.340
to become the most evil villain in the world!

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:49.590
Being evil means I don't have 
to be tied down by anyone!

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:53.350
I am free!

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.850
Did I take it too far this time?

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.060
With luck, he might barely be aliv—

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.920
So you're still dragging childhood 
trauma around with you?

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:13.220
Now I understand. You've always been

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:14.620
simple-minded.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.240
You hardened the water using Slow Down,

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.350
then used Speed Up to launch it at me?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.460
Isn't your Oath of Time an old model?!

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:26.580
How can you use Speed Up and 
Slow Down simultaneously?!

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.040
Did you think I wouldn't 
have made preparations

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:31.370
before coming to a seedy place like this?

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.120
Forgive me.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.440
I swapped my Oath of Time

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:52.490
with the newer model that Mina had.

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:57.280
My intention was to limit her 
power if it became necessary,

00:07:57.820 --> 00:08:00.220
but it proved useful in ways I didn't expect.

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.560
Now that's fun! That's really damn fun!

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.480
It's been ages since I got 
to play a game this exciting!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:23.810
True Rain of a Thousand Camps

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:35.860
Isn't the destructive power of a water blade
solidified with Slow Down incredible?

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:41.160
Fire can't be solidified like water,
after all, since it isn't a physical object.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.180
You can't defend against it.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.370
Not half bad.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:50.130
Defeating you will bring me a step closer 
to being the most evil villain in the world!

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:52.010
Stubborn fool!

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.470
Speed Up!

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:54.840
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:56.930
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:03.080
<i>If his Speed Up surpasses 
my Slow Down in strength,</i>

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:05.360
<i>my blade of solidified water will evaporate.</i>

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:06.980
<i>He's strong!</i>

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:11.580
<i>Is one's power as a Chronos Ruler 
proportionate to the strength of his will?</i>

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:16.160
<i>The best Slow Down I can 
manage right now is 1/2,700.</i>

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:20.500
<i>But the strength of his will 
clearly surpasses that!</i>

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:22.330
<i>I'm running low on spare water.</i>

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:24.330
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:29.690
My ambition is to become 
the world's #1 villain!

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:30.710
What about you?

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:34.730
I won't ever lose to a guy 
who doesn't even have a goal!

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:37.810
<i>A goal...</i>

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:44.710
I do have one!

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:48.470
Victor's time...

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.040
To get his time back is my goal!

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:56.820
To achieve that, I'll take down 
any enemy standing in my path!

00:09:58.590 --> 00:10:00.170
You're in this for someone else?

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:03.080
You can't beat me with 
sanctimonious drivel like that!

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:05.570
It's not for him!

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:07.720
There are a million things 
I want to say to him.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:12.760
But I'm the only one who remembers any of it.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:15.530
They're all memories he's lost.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:18.550
Right now, even though Victor is my father,

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:21.090
he's a complete stranger to me!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.810
Your father?

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.360
Victor is your father?

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:35.410
A villain like you wouldn't understand

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:39.860
what it's like when your own father's age
regresses until he's become a total stranger.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:44.610
No, someone who means 
even less to you than that!

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:50.350
What the hell, man?

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:53.500
I didn't know you had such a tragic past!

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.400
Huh?

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.540
Master's such an idiot.

00:10:57.540 --> 00:11:00.480
She didn't tell me anything about that!

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:03.280
A-Are you... crying?

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:05.760
Moron! Villains don't cry!

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.020
This is sweat! I'm just hot 
from controlling all that fire!

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.840
Anyway, I get it now!

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:14.750
The bad guy making you suffer is the 
Horologue that devoured Victor's time, right?

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:18.280
I'll beat up that jerk and 
become more evil than it is!

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:23.200
For you... no, for the sake of my ambition,
I'll kill that Horologue!

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:27.010
So don't let anyone else 
beat you until then, okay?

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:29.680
I'm the only one who's 
allowed to pick on you!

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:32.240
<i>He's...</i>

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:36.710
<i>...really still the good kid, Boy A.</i>

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:39.550
That settles it!

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.550
Starting today, you're my little brother!

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:43.140
Huh?!

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:45.010
We're blood brothers!

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:49.480
Starting today, I'm gonna look 
after you as your big brother!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:50.310
Are you nuts?

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:51.950
I'm serious!

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:53.500
Look, I don't even care.

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:57.190
If you're not going to fight anymore,
then get out of my way.

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:01.500
I don't have time to play 
along with your weird jokes.

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:06.070
Your master is trying 
to kill Victor right now.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:10.140
Huh? What're you talking about? 
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:13.170
The master never had any 
intention of killing Victor.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:13.980
What?

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:19.130
In fact, she's probably repairing 
his broken UNIQUE right now.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:24.740
Of course, if she learned while fighting him

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.640
that he's not worthy of UNIQUE,

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.560
I can't guess what'll happen to him.

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:33.380
H-Hey! You okay, Little Bro?!

00:12:33.380 --> 00:12:34.680
Who did this to—

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.700
Oh, right. I did.

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:41.370
What do I do? Actually... wait...

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:05.930
Well? Is that all there is 
to <i>your</i> "true strength"?

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.180
Ace Shield!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.310
Do you think the same trick 
will work on me again?

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:14.140
Speed Up!

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:14.140
<b>Speed Up</b>

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:15.520
Slow Down!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:15.520
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:13:16.130 --> 00:13:18.900
Shallow tactics like that will
only lead to your pointless death.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:22.530
Maybe you really aren't good enough
to be entrusted with UNIQUE.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.410
<i>Why aren't they falling?</i>

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:32.450
<i>I offset the Speed Up effect on his cards!</i>

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:37.920
What's the meaning of this?

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:41.830
You were convinced that I'd used 
the same move a second time.

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:45.840
By then, you were already caught in my trap.

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:50.150
Not all of the cards I used were Sped Up.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:51.760
It applies what I explained earlier.

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:56.800
Normal cards with nothing done to them were 
layered over some of the Sped Up cards.

00:13:57.470 --> 00:13:59.660
When you used Slow Down on those,

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:01.980
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:02.230
the Sped Up cards were offset and fell,

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:02.070
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:02.150
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:06.430
but the normal cards were 
Slowed Down and held in place.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:10.580
In other words, the cards 
holding you in place

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:13.190
were Slowed Down by you yourself.

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:16.540
And there's one other thing I've learned.

00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:19.890
Your ability to control time is powerful,

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.980
but its area of effect is very small.

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:26.050
Three meters at most, I'd say.

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:30.150
In other words, as long as I 
don't go near you, I'm safe.

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.170
Oh, and while I'm at it, I should warn you...

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:35.310
That chain of cards holding you in place

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.010
have been Sped Up or Slowed Down at random.

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:41.700
If you can't tell which is which, 
you're better off just staying still.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:46.450
Now... I have five cards left.

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:47.410
But...

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:50.780
They're the strongest hand, 
a royal straight flush.

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:52.740
Darling!

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:55.870
Do you still want to continue this fight?

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:58.260
If you want to fold, now's the time.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:02.980
It's true that a royal straight 
flush is the strongest hand.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:04.300
But...

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:09.180
That's nothing more than 
a rule you humans made up!

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.310
Speed Up!

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:18.770
She's gone.

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:21.670
Did she force the chain to 
break with a super Speed Up?

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:26.630
But if she did, the Sped Up cards 
should've ripped her body apart, too.

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:31.400
In my veins flows the blood
of the god Chronos.

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:32.390
Where is she?!

00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:36.330
All things in creation are under my control.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:45.420
Flowers, wind, grass, rain...

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:47.360
How is she so fast?

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:49.550
My eyes can't even follow her!

00:15:49.980 --> 00:15:52.580
All things prostrate themselves before me,

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:55.770
and all commands I give them are absolute.

00:15:55.770 --> 00:16:00.020
That includes even the cells in my own body.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.020
<i>She used Speed Up on herself?!</i>

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:02.770
All

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:04.440
Things

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:05.940
in

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:07.860
Creation

00:16:09.510 --> 00:16:10.460
This is

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.610
the power of a god!

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:18.490
That's...

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:28.270
She's using the Baguazhang form
of the Tensho kata!

00:16:28.810 --> 00:16:30.690
Sister's secret finishing technique!

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:39.640
Coiled Dragon Twister

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:00.680
Darling!

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.790
You're more resilient than I thought.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:12.510
To think you avoided my 
finishing blow in your state.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:15.120
You blew my mind.

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:18.660
I can't believe you can control 
your own body's components.

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:23.080
No wonder you call yourself a god.

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:28.490
And if you're a god,
I need to pay my respects.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.690
You still wish to resist me?

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:33.810
Feel free to think of it 
as struggling in vain.

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:38.360
Either way, this will be the last game.

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:44.380
These are the four cards I have showing.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:51.050
What's this? I'm one ace short 
of my royal straight flush.

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:53.090
Where did I put my trump card?

00:17:57.540 --> 00:17:59.470
I won't fall for that.

00:17:59.950 --> 00:18:03.220
Drawing my attention to 
a major miscalculation,

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.350
or "misdirection," is a 
basic magician's technique.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:10.730
The longer I listen to you,
the deeper I fall into your trap...

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:14.730
In which case I need only finish 
you off before you finish.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:18.160
You're supposed to listen until 
people are finished talking!

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.740
For a god, you're awfully impatient.

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:22.720
Just keep talking.

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:23.660
Speed Up!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.640
<i>One, two...</i>

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:31.290
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:18:31.990 --> 00:18:33.590
<i>One, two...</i>

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:37.910
What's wrong? Finished already?

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:43.510
This wouldn't have been enough 
to deadlock you back in the day.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:45.720
What a shame.

00:18:46.110 --> 00:18:50.270
I supposed you aren't fit to 
possess UNIQUE, after all.

00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:53.020
<i>One, two... three!</i>

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:54.270
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:03.280
<i>He Slowed Down my right hand?!</i>

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:06.850
<i>How can a human control part of my body?</i>

00:19:07.760 --> 00:19:08.850
<i>Inconceivable!</i>

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.750
<i>Her speed after using that 
super Speed Up on herself</i>

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:16.420
<i>is probably several times faster 
than the speed of sound.</i>

00:19:17.730 --> 00:19:21.180
<i>It's impossible to track with 
a human's reaction speed.</i>

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:24.140
<i>So what I need to do</i>

00:19:24.670 --> 00:19:30.350
<i>is make it look like I'm controlling 
her time, and her body itself.</i>

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:33.130
<i>The brief opening that gives me</i>

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:35.470
<i>might not even amount to half a second.</i>

00:19:36.470 --> 00:19:37.240
<i>But...</i>

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:48.290
It's more than enough time 
to finish this fight.

00:19:58.620 --> 00:20:00.050
So that's it.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:04.370
My right hand, my body itself,

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:06.540
wasn't under your control at all.

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:10.390
It was just the effect of 
your Slowed Down cards.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:14.650
Mere fragments of ripped ones, at that.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.160
Exactly.

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:21.040
I planted them in your right arm 
when you went for the final strike.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:26.990
Even in pieces, they're still 
cards under my control.

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:32.390
All that was left was to activate 
Slow Down at the right instant.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:35.600
It wasn't as easy as I make it sound, though.

00:20:37.490 --> 00:20:39.780
It's pointless if I'm too far from you,

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:41.930
but coming too close will get me killed.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:44.430
This battle was literally 
fought on a hair's breadth.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:48.220
Thankfully, though your attacks 
were fast, they were monotonous.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:52.050
In that sense, luck was on my side.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:57.340
That's why it's in your best interest to 
listen until people are finished talking.

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:01.690
Didn't I tell you at the start?

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:05.070
The ace is my trump card.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:11.080
So, I guess our showdown is over now.

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:12.750
Darling!

00:21:17.850 --> 00:21:21.750
<i>If Victor hadn't stopped his 
hand on that last attack,</i>

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:24.520
<i>it unquestionably would have killed me.</i>

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:29.200
Very well.

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:34.150
I acknowledge that you are 
worthy of possessing UNIQUE.

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:44.780
Welcome home,

00:21:46.520 --> 00:21:47.350
Victor.

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:51.450
Beyond Good and Evil

